# sudoers rule for the Xymon "claude" extension: lets the xymon user run
# claude-expiry.sh as root, which prints the login expiry of the named
# account and never any token.
#
# Install with visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/xymon-claude (FreeBSD:
# /usr/local/etc/sudoers.d/xymon-claude). Keep one uncommented line per
# account, with the path of YOUR platform: the user name in the rule is
# what limits it to those accounts. Hosts where the client runs as root
# need no rule - set CLAUDE_SUDO="no" there.
#
# The helper, and every directory above it, must not be writable by the
# xymon user - otherwise it could replace the helper and run anything as
# root. The packages install it root-owned below /usr (the rpm in
# /usr/libexec, whatever its client directory); a Xymon built from the
# sources makes its client directory and ext/ belong to the xymon user
# ("make install" chowns them), see below.

# Debian/Ubuntu (deb package) - the default account:
xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh root

# Rocky/EL with the rpm of this repository - any client directory,
# also one built with RPM_XYMONHOME (the rpm keeps the helper out of
# the client's ext/):
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/my-xymon-extensions/claude-expiry.sh root

# FreeBSD (net-mgmt/xymon-client):
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/www/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh root

# A client built from the sources and installed WITHOUT a package (the
# extension copied by hand into e.g. /home/xymon/client/ext): that
# directory belongs to the xymon user, so do NOT point a rule there.
# Copy the helper to a directory only root can write, and name that
# copy in the rule and in CLAUDE_HELPER (claude.cfg):
#   install -o root -g root -m 0755 /home/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh \
#       /usr/local/libexec/claude-expiry.sh
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/claude-expiry.sh root

# Further accounts: one line each, and add them to CLAUDE_ACCOUNTS:
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh deploy
#
# Never write the rule without the argument - that allows every account.
